      "side": 1,
      "message": "The fact that the modes are currently in an array in blk-crypto.c is an implementation detail.  This should be documented in a way that describes behavior, not implementation (though it can refer to the implementation, it shouldn\u0027t be the main point).  Maybe:\n\n * @key: Pointer to the bytes of the key to program. Must be the correct length\n *      for the chosen @crypt_mode; see blk_crypt_modes in blk-crypto.c.\n * @crypt_mode: Identifier for the encryption algorithm to use.",
