        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-03T22:17:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This logic is also duplicated at the end of the function.  IMO, it should be consolidated at the end like this:\n\n have_slot:\n        if (WARN_ON(atomic_read(\u0026ksm-\u003eslot_refs[slot]) \u003d\u003d UINT_MAX)) {\n                err \u003d -EBUSY;\n                goto out_unlock;\n        }\n        if (atomic_fetch_inc(\u0026ksm-\u003eslot_refs[slot]) \u003d\u003d 0)\n                atomic_dec(\u0026ksm-\u003enum_idle_slots);\n        ksm-\u003elast_used_seq_nums[slot] \u003d ++ksm-\u003eseq_num;\n out_unlock:\n        mutex_unlock(\u0026ksm-\u003elock);\n        return slot;\n\nThen this part would be:\n\n        slot \u003d ksm-\u003eksm_ll_ops.keyslot_find(ksm-\u003ell_priv_data, key,\n                                            data_unit_size, crypto_alg_id);\n        if (slot !\u003d -ENOKEY) {\n                if (slot \u003c 0)\n                        goto out_unlock;\n                if (WARN_ON(slot \u003e\u003d ksm-\u003enum_slots)) {\n                        slot \u003d -EINVAL;\n                        goto out_unlock;\n                }\n                goto have_slot;\n        }",
      "range": {
