      "message": "This return value here is unnecessary since the caller must already have a reference to the keyslot.  So it would be simpler to just return void and check for incorrect usage in here.\n\nvoid keyslot_manager_get_slot(struct keyslot_manager *ksm, unsigned int slot)\n{\n        if (WARN_ON(slot \u003e\u003d ksm-\u003enum_slots))\n                return;\n\n        WARN_ON(atomic_inc_return(\u0026ksm-\u003eslot_refs[slot]) \u003c 2); \n}\n\nSee ihold() for an example of an existing function in the kernel that works the same way.",
