    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ef8fbc9c_992fbb76",
        "filename": "include/linux/blk_types.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-03T22:17:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think these flags are actually necessary.\n\nBIO_CRYPT_ENABLED: use a flag REQ_INLINECRYPT in -\u003ebi_opf instead (similar to REQ_INTEGRITY).  One advantage of this is that bio_clone_crypt_ctx() becomes simpler -- you only need to actually copy the bio_crypt_ctx if the REQ_INLINECRYPT flag is set.\n\nBIO_CRYPT_SWHANDLED: AFAICS, this can be replaced with checking for processing_ksm \u003d\u003d blk_crypto_ksm, and this is only needed in blk-crypto.c.\n\nBIO_CRYPT_KEYSLOT: Just use -1 to mean an unset keyslot, and \u003e\u003d 0 to mean a set keyslot.  IIRC, I suggested against this earlier because at the time it was the means for determining whether encryption was enabled, and having the initial value of 0 be \"encryption disabled\" was desirable.  But now that a separate \"enabled\" flag is needed anyway, keyslot \u003d -1 works fine since it can be set at the same time the flag is set.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 140,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 149,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "762d0068f4912f6f7e9b63855bdd77afb6d4d922",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
