      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-03T22:17:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is a \u0027crypto_alg_id\u0027 exactly?  According to this it represents a crypt_mode and a data_unit_size.  But actually it doesn\u0027t, because the other keyslot_mgmt_ll_ops methods still take the crypto_alg_id and data_unit_size separately.  It seems this is because you use UFS crypto capability index directly as the crypto_alg_id.  But couldn\u0027t the crypto_alg_id for UFS just encode both the data_unit_size and capability index, like (data_unit_size \u003c\u003c 16) | cap_idx?  Otherwise, I don\u0027t see much point in having crypto_alg_id at all, as opposed to using crypt_mode directly.",
      "range": {
